# 9. Your dataset is NOT yet a perfect ML dataset

This is very important.

Looking at your CSV, I can see that it contains **raw literature extraction information** as well as fields intended for ML.

For example, the first Lewis row contains:

```text
Hepatocyte_viability:
High; numeric value not reported in text

Albumin:
~40 pg/cell more cumulative albumin secretion than 90°

CYP3A4:
3D activity significantly higher than 2D;
numeric value not reported
```

These are scientifically useful, but they are **not directly usable as numerical ML targets**.

For example:

```text
"High"
```

cannot directly be used as:

```text
91%
```

unless the paper actually reports 91%.

Similarly:

```text
"~40 pg/cell more"
```

is not the same thing as:

```text
Albumin = 40 pg/mL
```

So your dataset currently contains **literature-extracted evidence**, not just clean numerical ML data.

That distinction is extremely important.

